From 1fdfbe624dc72003ed39c7abad5b99521f38c78a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:28:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0007: tear-free MDP flips and fit-to-screen on
 jasmine

With topaz's MDP code guarded off, jasmine copied every frame straight into
the boot framebuffer the panel scans (tearing). ADT /sweet-mdp gives the
SDM660 MDP and two back buffers inside the firmware's splash reservation
(below 4 GiB, which the MDP needs and XNU's RAM is not). At start the pipe
fetching the boot framebuffer (VIG0/VIG1/DMA0-2) and the CTL staging it are
found and logged; frames are composed into the back buffer (write-combined)
and flipped with SSPP_SRC0_ADDR + CTL_FLUSH, as topaz does with VIG0/CTL0.
sweetmdp=0 keeps the old copy. The console keeps drawing into the boot
framebuffer, which a panic scans out again.

Fit: the 1125x2436 frame is scaled uniformly (nearest sample) to the panel
height, 997x2160 centred, instead of cropping the status bar and home
indicator; SweetHIDTouch maps touches through the same fit. sweetfb_fit=0
crops as before.
---
